How can I modify the following C++ code to create a program that generates a Fibonacci sequence up to a user-defined limit and then displays the sequence in reverse order? 
Here is the initial code:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main() {
  int n, t1 = 0, t2 = 1, nextTerm = 0;
  cout << "Enter the number of terms: ";
  cin >> n;
  cout << "Fibonacci Series: ";
  for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
      // Prints the first two terms.
      if(i == 1) {
          cout << " " << t1;
          continue;
      }
      if(i == 2) {
          cout << t2 << " ";
          continue;
      }
      nextTerm = t1 + t2;
      t1 = t2;
      t2 = nextTerm;

      cout << nextTerm << " ";
  }
  return 0;
} 
In addition to generating the Fibonacci sequence in reverse order, the program should also prompt the user for a limit and ensure that the input is valid (i.e., a positive integer). Finally, the program should display the sequence in a visually appealing way, such as in a table or chart.

